+# [MP8] Score multipliers per minigame (default 1.0, only the ones that need lowering/raising are listed).
+#
+# Duck Hunt is 0.5 because it's "everyone takes a turn as hunter". 8 players with two hunters = **4 sub-rounds**, and the scores add up.
+# After switching to placement scoring + points for hits, a single match can reach 0~42, while placement minigames (the Disco Dodge kind) only reach 0~16,
+# so Duck Hunt would dominate.
+# The upside of putting the multiplier **where scores are totaled** is that each minigame's own placement rules stay untouched,
+# and future balance tweaks only change this one table, without going back into gameplay code.
+# (Decided by the user 2026-08-15 - Duck Hunt 50%)
+const MP8_MINIGAME_SCORE_SCALE: Dictionary = {
+	Globals.MinigameIdentifier.DuckHunt: 0.5,
+	# Exploding Collar Race's score scale grew after switching to placement scoring (user decision 2026-08-16, derivation in exploding_collar_race.gd).
+	#   Vanilla additive scoring, 8 players = per-round max 4 points × 3 rounds = 0~12
+	#   Placement scoring,        8 players = per-round max 8 points (placement 0~7 + full health 1) × 3 rounds = **0~24**
+	# Meanwhile placement family A (Disco Dodge) is 0~16 for 8 players over 2 rounds. Exploding Collar Race plays 3 rounds, so it should weigh a bit more,
+	# but double is too much — ×0.75 → **0~18**, about 12% above family A, which lines up with "one extra round".
+	Globals.MinigameIdentifier.ExplodingCollarRace: 0.75,
+}
+
+# The same minigame plays a different number of rounds at different player counts, so its weight can vary a lot too. That's why there's another "per player count override" layer.
+#
+# Duck Hunt at 6 players is 0.8 because Duck Hunt's sub-round count = players ÷ hunters per round,
+# and 6 players with two hunters is only **3 sub-rounds** (8 players is 4), with each player being a duck only 2 times.
+# That works out to an expected 5 points with a range of 0~10, lighter even than placement minigames at the same player count (about 0~12),
+# which is the exact opposite of its role in 8-player matches. Raising it to 0.8 brings this tier back in line.
+# (Decided by the user 2026-08-15)
+const MP8_MINIGAME_SCORE_SCALE_BY_COUNT: Dictionary = {
+	Globals.MinigameIdentifier.DuckHunt: {6: 0.8},
+}
+
+
