+# =============== [MP8] Restart-this-round vote ===============
+#
+# Why this feature exists (requested by the user 2026-09-03, this section is the design record).
+# This mod expands 4 players to 8. 15 minigames x 5~8 players = 60 combinations, more than the author can verify alone
+# — and 8 real people are hard to get together. "Whole match stuck" has happened many times, e.g. Junk Platform 8-player matches never ending,
+# Spine Breaker devices latching onto someone without biting, and someone in Duck Hunt getting no response from wasd.
+#
+# This feature **fixes no bugs**. It does two things.
+#   ① Stop the bleeding: when stuck, a majority of the lobby can restart this round without leaving and starting over
+#   ② **Evidence**: every restart is forced to log one line (which minigame, how many players, which round).
+#      This is worth more than the restart itself — it turns "the author can't test it all" into "players flag what's broken for you".
+#      When a "XX got stuck" report comes in, grep `[MP8-RESTART]` first.
+#
+# Design trade-offs (decided by the user)
+#   · Only go back to **the start of this round**, not round 1 of the minigame (that would also need game_score rolled back)
+#   · A **majority** is enough, not n-1. The stuck player might be exactly the one who can't press keys,
+#     and a single AFK player would make n-1 impossible forever
+#   · Once a majority is reached it doesn't run immediately. An **auto-confirm countdown** runs first so everyone gets a heads-up. Withdrawing a vote during it cancels
+#   · Two entry points: F5 and the button in the ESC menu. The ESC one is the main entry —
+#     while the menu is open the UI eats key presses, so F5 might not get through (which is also why the user specifically asked for a button)
+#
+# Why the timing is safe. Every round already goes through load_minigame(id, true)
+# (see _on_minigame_finished in minigame_playing_state.gd), so "restart this round"
+# and "go to the next round" are **the same path**, not newly invented teardown logic. Clients don't need a separate notification either —
+# host_loaded runs _host_minigame_loaded_rpc on its own.
+#
+# Why scores must be rolled back. round_score_by_network_id is added to in **two** places —
+# _on_minigame_player_scored (adds on every score mid-round) and _on_minigame_player_score_finalized
+# (end-of-round settle). Restarting mid-round without rolling back would keep that partial score, and replaying would count it twice.
+# So load_minigame takes a snapshot at its start, and a restart restores it.
+
+const MP8_VOTE_KEY: int = KEY_F5              # F1/F2/F9 are taken by vanilla debug keys, F5 is free
+const MP8_VOTE_COUNTDOWN: float = 5.0         # Auto-confirm countdown after a majority (seconds)
+
+# — Server-authoritative state —
